# Witherbloom Command, modes 1 and 2, aimed at its caster's own side: "target player" may be you, and the land card returned
# may be one just milled (ruling 2021-04-16). Bot1 mills itself three (Forest, Swamp, Mind Stone) and returns the Forest,
# leaving the Swamp in the graveyard; "noncreature, nonland permanent with mana value 2 or less" accepts Bot1's own Mox Ruby
# (mana value 0), destroyed. Bot2's Mox Pearl (also mana value 0) stays: only the target is destroyed.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Witherbloom Command
Island x3
Forest
Swamp
Mind Stone
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Witherbloom Command.Cast
Bot1.Modes(1; 2)
Bot1.Target(Bot1)
Bot1.Target(Mox Ruby)
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
? Bot1.Mana = 
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Forest)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Island; Island; Island
Bot1.Graveyard = Witherbloom Command; Mox Ruby; Mind Stone; Swamp
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Tapped = true
